# Commit / deploy policy — only #1 commits

All sessions share ONE working copy at `C:\dev\CCH-Platform-Deploy\cch-deploy`. A commit here
sweeps up **every session's** uncommitted edits, and a deploy ships them all. So:

## Do NOT (any session except #1)
- Do NOT run `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, `git stash`, or anything that stages/commits.
- Do NOT run any `firebase deploy` (hosting, functions, rules) — staging OR production.

## Do
- Edit your files normally.
- When ready, **append one line to `_DEPLOY_QUEUE.md`** (repo root) instead of messaging Cindy:
  `[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] #<n> <name> — <files changed> — <staging|production> — <one-line desc> — STATUS: pending`
- #1 (Deploy Master) reads `_DEPLOY_QUEUE.md` **hourly (automation)** and on demand, then commits/deploys
  in coordinated batches and flips your line to `STATUS: done`.
- `git pull` / `git fetch` / read-only `git status` are fine.

## Staging vs production
- **Staging** (`cch-platform-staging.web.app`) is a safe test sandbox — **no per-deploy approval from
  Cindy needed**. #1 deploys queued staging items, serialized so staging stays readable (one session's
  work at a time). Just queue it.
- **Production** (`cch-platform.web.app`) ships **only on Cindy's explicit typed GO**.

Only **#1** commits and deploys.
